 | `find-slice-gaps` | List each thing a slice needs that neither the model nor memory answers, and write each as one question by the rule for asking a person (id, topic, question, why, examples from several domains, blocking, assume, settled with its basis); never the surface or the tester. Rewrite mode rewrites only the questions the play's script refuses. Writes `questions.json`. | /design-slice |
 | `author-slice` | Choose the slice: the one surface and its tester (a persona), the features from any capability in build order, what is left out, and the needs list (`fills.json`: new parts, updates, thin parts); `no-slice.json` when no surface can be tested end to end. Reuse mode writes `reuse.json` (pull in, push out); fix mode fixes `slice.json` or `fills.json`; edit mode turns a person's edit words into `edit-list.json` (each change's record, part, old and new text, and the records made out of date). Never writes the model. | /design-slice |
 | `enrich-grounding` | Write on the pages of the model's parts, in place, keeping every section and line: bring a domain, capability or feature page up to the current rules, write one new feature under a capability that exists, write a thin ICE (Goal, Limit, Fails if, Context, Checked by), change the named lines of any page — domain, capability, feature or intent — through its `change_lines.py` (all or nothing; #993), write a page a person approved word for word — a domain, capability or feature page, or an ICE page `ice.md` — through its `write_approved.py` (all or nothing; #1031), fix the pages the model check names. Never writes `_spine.yaml` or the thin marks. | /design-slice; a part found during work (#979), before `link-model-part`; named lines of any page (#993); approved pages (#1031) |
